[342.219149, "o", "\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[G\r\n\u001b[38;5;231m●\u001b[39m I can see the fixture shows a standard span structure. Based on the error analysis, the issue is that the Sentry API\r\n  can return a mixed array containing both span objects (like in the fixture) AND issue objects that don't have all the\r\n  required span fields. Let me update the todos and implement the fix:\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;5;174m*\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;174mAnalyzing \u001b[38;5;216mthe\u001b[38;5;174m schema mismatch… \u001b[39m\u001b[2m(esc to interrupt · /todos)\u001b[22m\r\n  ⎿  \u001b[2mNext: Implement fix to handle mixed span/issue arrays from API\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m│\u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;246m > \u001b[39m                                                                                                                       \u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m│\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;147m⏵⏵ accept edits on\u001b[38;5;246m\u001b[2m (shift+tab to cycle)\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\r\n"]
