[542.19797, "o", "\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;5;114m●\u001b[39m \u001b[1mRead\u001b[22m(packages/mcp-server/src/tools/get-trace-details.ts)\r\n  ⎿  Read \u001b[1m100\u001b[22m lines \u001b[38;5;246m(ctrl+r to expand)\u001b[39m\u001b(B\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;5;114m●\u001b[39m \u001b[1mRead\u001b[22m(packages/mcp-server/src/tools/get-trace-details.ts)\r\n  ⎿  Read \u001b[1m150\u001b[22m lines \u001b[38;5;246m(ctrl+r to expand)\u001b[39m\u001b(B\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;5;231m●\u001b[39m I can see that the \u001b[38;5;153mselectInterestingSpans\u001b[39m function processes the trace data. It's expecting spans with certain\r\n  properties. Now I need to update it to handle the mixed array. Let me check where and how the trace is passed to this\r\n  function:\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;5;114m●\u001b[39m \u001b[1mSearch\u001b[22m(pattern: \"selectInterestingSpans|formatTraceOutput\", path: \"packages/mcp-server/src/tools/get-trace-details.ts\",\r\n        output_mode: \"content\")\r\n  ⎿  Found \u001b[1m27 \u001b[22mlines \u001b[38;5;246m(ctrl+r to expand)\u001b[39m\u001b(B\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;5;231m●\u001b[39m Now I see the issue. The \u001b[38;5;153mselectInterestingSpans\u001b[39m function is being passed the \u001b[38;5;153mtrace\u001b[39m array directly, which may contain\r\n  both spans and issues. I need to filter out the issues before processing. Let me update the function:\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;5;114m●\u001b[39m \u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(packages/mcp-server/src/tools/get-trace-details.ts)\r\n  ⎿  Updated \u001b[1mpackages/mcp-server/src/tools/get-trace-details.ts\u001b[22m with \u001b[1m10\u001b[22m additions          \u001b(B\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  152 \u001b[38;5;231m     const selected: SelectedSpan[] = [];\u001b[39m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  153 \u001b[38;5;231m     let spanCount = 0;\u001b[39m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  154 \u001b[38;5;231m   \u001b[39m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  155 \u001b[48;5;65m\u001b[38;5;231m+    // Filter out non-span items (issues) from the trace data\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  156 \u001b[48;5;65m\u001b[38;5;231m+    // Spans must have children array, duration, and other span-specific fields\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  157 \u001b[48;5;65m\u001b[38;5;231m+    const actualSpans = spans.filter(item => \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  158 \u001b[48;5;65m\u001b[38;5;231m+      item && \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  159 \u001b[48;5;65m\u001b[38;5;231m+      typeof item === 'object' && \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  160 \u001b[48;5;65m\u001b[38;5;231m+      'children' in item &&\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  161 \u001b[48;5;65m\u001b[38;5;231m+      Array.isArray(item.children) &&\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  162 \u001b[48;5;65m\u001b[38;5;231m+      'duration' in item\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  163 \u001b[48;5;65m\u001b[38;5;231m+    );\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  164 \u001b[48;5;65m\u001b[38;5;231m+  \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  165 \u001b[38;5;231m     function addSpan(span: any, level: number): boolean {\u001b[39m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  166 \u001b[38;5;231m       if (spanCount >= maxSpans || level > MAX_DEPTH) return false;\u001b[39m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  167 \u001b[38;5;231m   \u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;5;114m●\u001b[39m \u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(packages/mcp-server/src/tools/get-trace-details.ts)\r\n  ⎿  Updated \u001b[1mpackages/mcp-server/src/tools/get-trace-details.ts\u001b[22m with \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m addition and \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m removal\u001b(B\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  219 \u001b[38;5;231m     }\u001b[39m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  220 \u001b[38;5;231m   \u001b[39m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  221 \u001b[38;5;231m     // Sort root spans by duration and select the most interesting ones\u001b[39m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m  222 \u001b[39m\u001b[48;5;95m-  \u001b[38;5;231m  const sortedRoots = \u001b[48;5;174mspans\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;24