[554.967742, "o", "\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[G\r\n\u001b[38;5;174m*\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;174mPollinating… \u001b[39m\u001b[2m(esc to interrupt)\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m│\u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;246m > \u001b[39m                                                                                                                       \u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m│\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;147m⏵⏵ accept edits on\u001b[38;5;246m\u001b[2m (shift+tab to cycle)\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[555.118131, "o", "\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[G\r\n\u001b[38;5;174m✢\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;174mPollinating… \u001b[39m\u001b[2m(esc to interrupt)\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m│\u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;246m > \u001b[39m                                                                                                                       \u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m│\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;147m⏵⏵ accept edits on\u001b[38;5;246m\u001b[2m (shift+tab to cycle)\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[555.169994, "o", "\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[G\r\n\u001b[38;5;231m●\u001b[39m \u001b[1mSummary\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  I've successfully fixed the issue \u001b[38;5;153mhttps://sentry.sentry.io/issues/6811213890/\u001b[39m in the Sentry MCP codebase. The problem\r\n  was that the \u001b[38;5;153mTraceSchema\u001b[39m expected all items in the trace response to be \u001b[38;5;153mTraceSpanSchema\u001b[39m objects, but the Sentry API\r\n  can return a mixed array containing both span objects and issue objects.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[2mChanges Made:\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  1. \u001b[1mUpdated \u001b[38;5;153mpackages/mcp-server/src/api-client/schema.ts\u001b[39m\u001b[22m:\r\n    - Added a new \u001b[38;5;153mTraceIssueSchema\u001b[39m to handle issue objects that can appear in trace responses\r\n    - Modified \u001b[38;5;153mTraceSchema\u001b[39m to accept a union of both \u001b[38;5;153mTraceSpanSchema\u001b[39m and \u001b[38;5;153mTraceIssueSchema\u001b[39m\r\n  2. \u001b[1mUpdated \u001b[38;5;153mpackages/mcp-server/src/api-client/types.ts\u001b[39m\u001b[22m:\r\n    - Added the \u001b[38;5;153mTraceIssueSchema\u001b[39m export\r\n    - Created the \u001b[38;5;153mTraceIssue\u001b[39m type\r\n  3. \u001b[1mUpdated \u001b[38;5;153mpackages/mcp-server/src/tools/get-trace-details.ts\u001b[39m\u001b[22m:\r\n    - Modified \u001b[38;5;153mselectInterestingSpans\u001b[39m to filter out non-span items (issues) before processing\r\n    - Modified \u001b[38;5;153mgetAllSpansFlattened\u001b[39m to also filter out non-span items\r\n\r\n  \u001b[2mRoot Cause:\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  The Sentry API's \u001b[38;5;153mquery_trace_data\u001b[39m function returns a heterogeneous array containing both \u001b[38;5;153mSerializedSpan\u001b[39m and\r\n  \u001b[38;5;153mSerializedIssue\u001b[39m objects when there are errors not directly associated with spans. The client's schema was too strict\r\n  and only expected span objects.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[2mSolution:\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  The fix allows the schema to handle both types of objects in the trace response, and the processing functions now\r\n  filter out issue objects when working with spans to prevent runtime errors.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[2mValidation:\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n  - ✅ TypeScript compilation passes\r\n  - ✅ Linting passes (except for pre-existing large fixture file warning)\r\n  - ✅ All mcp-server tests pass (292 tests passing)\r\n\r\n  The fix addresses the ZodError validation failures and allows the MCP server to properly handle trace responses that\r\n  contain both spans and standalone issue objects.\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;5;174m✢\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;174mPollinating… \u001b[39m\u001b[2m(esc to interrupt)\u001b[22m\r\n\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m│\u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;246m > \u001b[39m                                                                                                                       \u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m│\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;147m⏵⏵ accept edits on\u001b[38;5;246m\u001b[2m (shift+tab to cycle)\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[555.194115, "o", "\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[G\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m│\u001b[39m\u001b[22m >                                                                                                                        \u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m│\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[38;5;244m╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;147m⏵⏵ accept edits on\u001b[38;5;246m\u001b[2m (shift+tab to cycle)\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\r\n"]
